WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.960
Season Four
of Stranger Things

00:00:02.044 --> 00:00:04.087
arrives on Netflix
later this year.

00:00:04.171 --> 00:00:06.423
But how has the cast been
keeping themselves busy

00:00:06.507 --> 00:00:08.383
in the gap between seasons?

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:11.345
Voice acting, music videos,
Netflix Originals,

00:00:11.428 --> 00:00:13.639
Hollywood blockbusters,
you name it?

00:00:13.722 --> 00:00:15.724
Here's what the kids
from Stranger things

00:00:15.807 --> 00:00:16.725
have been up to.

00:00:23.607 --> 00:00:25.526
Millie Bobby Brown,
who plays

00:00:25.609 --> 00:00:27.653
the psychokinetically
gifted Eleven,

00:00:27.736 --> 00:00:30.531
starred in stacks
of high-profile productions

00:00:30.614 --> 00:00:32.241
between seasons
of Stranger Things.

00:00:32.324 --> 00:00:35.702
Most notably, she played the
title role in Enola Holmes,

00:00:35.786 --> 00:00:37.871
a 2020
Netflix Original mystery

00:00:37.955 --> 00:00:39.665
based on the books
by Nancy Springer.

00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:41.542
In case
you somehow missed it,

00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:43.710
it's a sassy,
energetic spin-off

00:00:43.794 --> 00:00:46.004
from the classic stories
by Arthur Conan Doyle,

00:00:46.088 --> 00:00:47.840
which details the adventures
of Holmes'

00:00:47.923 --> 00:00:49.216
lesser-known little sister.

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:52.094
A second Enola Holmes film
is in post-production,

00:00:52.177 --> 00:00:55.097
with Bobby Brown returning
alongside Louis Partridge.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:56.932
Millie also found time
to feature

00:00:57.015 --> 00:00:59.685
in 2019's Godzilla:
King of the Monsters

00:00:59.768 --> 00:01:03.063
and in the 2021 sequel,
Godzilla vs. Kong,

00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:05.190
and there are
other interesting roles

00:01:05.274 --> 00:01:06.525
on the horizon.

00:01:06.608 --> 00:01:08.485
She'll star in
and executive produce

00:01:08.569 --> 00:01:09.862
2023's Damsel,

00:01:09.945 --> 00:01:12.197
another Netflix Original
that subverts

00:01:12.281 --> 00:01:13.740
the damsel-in-distress trope

00:01:13.824 --> 00:01:15.701
and sees Bobby Brown's
Princess Elodie

00:01:15.784 --> 00:01:18.996
taking on a dragon rather
than waiting to be rescued.

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:21.123
Seems Eleven's not
the only one capable

00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:24.001
of laying the smack down
on terrifying monsters.

00:01:27.045 --> 00:01:28.797
Finn Wolfhard,
who plays Mike Wheeler,

00:01:28.881 --> 00:01:30.883
has likewise been
keeping himself active

00:01:30.966 --> 00:01:32.968
with some
high-profile releases.

00:01:33.051 --> 00:01:34.469
In 2017's It,

00:01:34.553 --> 00:01:37.055
he played the younger
version of Richie Tozier

00:01:37.139 --> 00:01:39.850
in this chilling adaptation
of the Stephen King novel.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:41.685
And more recently,
he starred

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.937
in 2021's
Ghostbusters: Afterlife,

00:01:44.021 --> 00:01:46.398
a follow-up to
the Ivan Reitman originals

00:01:46.481 --> 00:01:49.234
directed and co-written
by his son Jason.

00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:52.404
In it, Finn plays
Trevor Spengler,

00:01:52.487 --> 00:01:55.490
grandson of the late
Harold Ramis's Egon,

00:01:55.574 --> 00:01:57.576
who gets to live out our
collective childhood dream

00:01:57.659 --> 00:01:59.369
of driving Ecto-1.

00:01:59.453 --> 00:02:01.914
It's a significant step up
from a pushbike

00:02:01.997 --> 00:02:03.582
and a Peter Venkman outfit.

00:02:03.665 --> 00:02:05.584
-Why are you Venkman?
-Because I'm Venkman.

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:06.627
No, I'm Venkman.

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:08.921
Alongside big-budget
Hollywood sequels,

00:02:09.004 --> 00:02:10.881
Wolfhard has done
plenty of voice work,

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.424
including Carmen Sandiego,

00:02:12.508 --> 00:02:14.218
in which he features
as Player,

00:02:14.301 --> 00:02:15.928
a teenage hacker
based on the unseen

00:02:16.011 --> 00:02:17.513
live-action character

00:02:17.596 --> 00:02:20.265
from the original
1994 animated series

00:02:20.349 --> 00:02:22.684
Where on Earth
is Carmen Sandiego?

00:02:22.768 --> 00:02:25.020
He also added
to his horror credentials

00:02:25.103 --> 00:02:27.314
by voicing the sinister
Pugsley Addams

00:02:27.397 --> 00:02:28.941
in 2019's The Addams Family,

00:02:29.024 --> 00:02:31.610
and he provided the voice
of Boypunzel

00:02:31.693 --> 00:02:33.445
in JJ Villard's Fairy Tales.

00:02:33.529 --> 00:02:35.697
Really? I didn't know that.

00:02:35.781 --> 00:02:38.325
More voice work
is on the horizon for 2022

00:02:38.408 --> 00:02:39.535
in Pinocchio,

00:02:39.618 --> 00:02:40.994
in which he plays Lampwick,

00:02:41.078 --> 00:02:43.205
as well as
The Legend of Ochi.

00:02:43.288 --> 00:02:44.790
He'll also star as Ziggy

00:02:44.873 --> 00:02:47.668
in 2022's When You Finish
Saving The World,

00:02:47.751 --> 00:02:50.254
Jesse Eisenberg's
directorial debut.

00:02:50.712 --> 00:02:52.840
Next we have
Gaten Matarazzo,

00:02:52.923 --> 00:02:53.924
who plays Dustin,

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:56.093
everyone's favourite
Demodog-raising

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:58.637
Neverending Story
duetting superstar.

00:03:01.974 --> 00:03:03.183
Beautiful.

00:03:03.267 --> 00:03:04.643
Like the rest of the cast,

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:06.603
Gaten has loads of stuff
on the go.

00:03:06.687 --> 00:03:08.397
He produces
Prank Encounters,

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.691
a horror-themed hidden
camera show on Netflix,

00:03:10.774 --> 00:03:12.150
and, like Finn Wolfhard,

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:13.986
he's been doing plenty
of VO work.

00:03:14.069 --> 00:03:17.823
He voiced Bubba in 2019's
The Angry Birds Movie 2

00:03:17.906 --> 00:03:19.616
and he'll play
the role of Ramy

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:22.286
in the 2022
animated feature Hump.

00:03:22.369 --> 00:03:24.872
Matarazzo also made
a cameo appearance

00:03:24.955 --> 00:03:26.415
as Casey the Electrician

00:03:26.498 --> 00:03:29.376
in Michelle Obama's adorable
cooking show for kids

00:03:29.459 --> 00:03:31.044
Waffles + Mochi.

00:03:31.128 --> 00:03:32.546
That's umami.

00:03:32.629 --> 00:03:34.047
-Umami!
-What about my mummy?

00:03:34.131 --> 00:03:36.175
He also uses his fame
to raise awareness

00:03:36.258 --> 00:03:38.719
about his condition,
cleidocranial dysplasia,

00:03:38.802 --> 00:03:40.137
as well as fundraising

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:43.140
for non-profit organisation
CCD Smiles.

00:03:43.974 --> 00:03:46.727
Caleb McLaughlin plays Lucas
in Stranger Things,

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:49.188
the most pragmatic member
of the group

00:03:49.271 --> 00:03:51.481
and undisputed master
of the wrist rocket.

00:03:53.859 --> 00:03:56.612
Like his co-stars,
he's been super proactive.

00:03:56.695 --> 00:04:00.365
He made his Hollywood debut
in 2020's Concrete Cowboy,

00:04:00.449 --> 00:04:02.117
directed by Ricky Staub

00:04:02.201 --> 00:04:04.661
and based on the novel
Ghetto Cowboy by Greg Neri.

00:04:04.745 --> 00:04:06.997
In it,
McLaughlin stars as Cole,

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.999
a Detroit teenager
sent to live

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:11.585
with his estranged father
Harp played by Idris Elba.

00:04:11.668 --> 00:04:13.587
-I'm your father.
-You ain't my father!

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:15.881
McLaughlin's performance
drew praise,

00:04:15.964 --> 00:04:17.633
and the story is based
on the real urban

00:04:17.716 --> 00:04:19.551
African American
horse riding culture

00:04:19.635 --> 00:04:20.594
of Philadelphia,

00:04:20.677 --> 00:04:23.889
specifically the Fletcher
Street Urban Riding Club.

00:04:23.972 --> 00:04:25.641
In 2019, McLaughlin appeared

00:04:25.724 --> 00:04:27.893
in Steven Soderbergh's
High Flying Bird,

00:04:27.976 --> 00:04:31.063
a sports drama detailing
the world of pro basketball,

00:04:31.146 --> 00:04:33.232
and he's also done
plenty of voice work.

00:04:33.315 --> 00:04:36.109
Featuring as young Gary
in Final Space,

00:04:36.193 --> 00:04:38.403
Ghost the Boy
in Summer Camp Island,

00:04:38.487 --> 00:04:41.156
and Trevor Johnson
in Ultra City Smiths.

00:04:41.615 --> 00:04:43.200
Noah Schnapp plays Will,

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:44.576
perhaps the most complex

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:46.620
and troubled member
of the party.

00:04:46.703 --> 00:04:48.914
A huge chunk of
his childhood goes missing

00:04:48.997 --> 00:04:51.041
and he spends a week
in the Upside Down

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:52.751
being hunted
by the Demogorgon.

00:04:52.835 --> 00:04:54.044
In 2018,

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:56.713
he played nine-year-old
crossword fanatic Otis

00:04:56.797 --> 00:04:58.590
in Donal Lardner Ward's
drama

00:04:58.674 --> 00:05:00.259
We Only Know So Much.

00:05:00.342 --> 00:05:03.136
And a year later he landed
the lead role in Abe,

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:04.555
a comedy about a boy

00:05:04.638 --> 00:05:06.640
who grows tired
of mealtime arguments

00:05:06.723 --> 00:05:08.892
and tries to reunite
his estranged

00:05:08.976 --> 00:05:11.270
half-Israeli,
half-Palestinian family

00:05:11.353 --> 00:05:13.021
via the medium of cooking.

00:05:13.105 --> 00:05:15.691
2020 saw him feature
in period drama

00:05:15.774 --> 00:05:18.318
Waiting for Anya,
in which he played Jo,

00:05:18.402 --> 00:05:19.862
a 13-year-old shepherd

00:05:19.945 --> 00:05:21.989
helping smuggle
Jewish children into Spain

00:05:22.072 --> 00:05:23.949
in an adaptation
of Michael Morpurgo's

00:05:24.032 --> 00:05:26.159
popular young adult novel
of the same name.

00:05:26.243 --> 00:05:27.119
You're a monster!

00:05:27.202 --> 00:05:29.872
And as if to prove
how versatile he is,

00:05:29.955 --> 00:05:32.583
Noah also featured
in 2020 comedy horror

00:05:32.666 --> 00:05:33.750
Hubie Halloween

00:05:33.834 --> 00:05:36.420
alongside none other
than Adam Sandler.

00:05:36.503 --> 00:05:38.463
Ghost, scary,

00:05:38.547 --> 00:05:41.258
but also the key
to Halloween safety.

00:05:41.884 --> 00:05:44.261
You'll know Sadie Sink
as tomboy Max,

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:47.264
the skateboarding,
Dig Dug-destroying outsider

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:49.766
who captures the hearts
of Dustin and Lucas

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:50.851
in Season 2.

00:05:50.934 --> 00:05:54.062
Aside from internet-breaking
Taylor Swift videos,

00:05:54.146 --> 00:05:55.564
her most recent appearance
was in

00:05:55.647 --> 00:05:57.399
Leigh Janiak's Fear Street.

00:05:57.482 --> 00:05:59.985
She played Ziggy Berman
in Part 2 of the trilogy,

00:06:00.068 --> 00:06:02.613
cementing her horror movie
final girl status

00:06:02.696 --> 00:06:05.073
in this bloody homage
to 70's horror.

00:06:05.157 --> 00:06:07.701
It wasn't her first foray
into the genre.

00:06:07.784 --> 00:06:10.704
In 2019, she appeared
as teenage nurse Haley

00:06:10.787 --> 00:06:12.581
-in Ciaran Foy's Eli…
-Boo!

00:06:12.664 --> 00:06:15.083
…a movie about
an autoimmune deficient boy

00:06:15.167 --> 00:06:16.835
receiving care in a secluded

00:06:16.919 --> 00:06:18.962
and sinister
medical facility.

00:06:19.046 --> 00:06:21.507
Looking ahead, Sadie
will play the lead role

00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:23.717
in 9/11 drama Dear Zoe,

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:25.469
as well as Ellie
in forthcoming

00:06:25.552 --> 00:06:28.013
Darren Aronofsky comedy
The Whale.

00:06:28.096 --> 00:06:30.349
That's not all.
Sink is a vegan

00:06:30.432 --> 00:06:32.726
and passionate
animal welfare activist.

00:06:32.809 --> 00:06:34.728
And in 2018,
she collaborated

00:06:34.811 --> 00:06:36.146
with the likes
of Rooney Mara,

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:38.440
Joaquin Phoenix
and Sia in Dominion,

00:06:38.524 --> 00:06:41.360
an animal rights documentary
from Chris Delforce,

00:06:41.443 --> 00:06:42.861
a performance
that would land her

00:06:42.945 --> 00:06:44.363
an Award of Excellence
for Narration

00:06:44.446 --> 00:06:45.906
from the Hollywood
International

00:06:45.989 --> 00:06:48.075
Independent
Documentary Awards.

00:06:48.825 --> 00:06:50.911
Priah Ferguson's
performance of Erica,

00:06:50.994 --> 00:06:53.330
Lucas's take-no-prisoners
younger sister,

00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:56.333
made her the breakout star
of Stranger Things Season 3.

00:06:56.917 --> 00:06:58.168
The scourge of Scoops Ahoy's

00:06:58.252 --> 00:06:59.545
free ice cream policy

00:06:59.628 --> 00:07:02.214
and frequent tormentor
of Steve Harrington.

00:07:02.756 --> 00:07:04.132
More fudge, please.

00:07:04.216 --> 00:07:05.968
And if you want to see
more of her,

00:07:06.051 --> 00:07:08.262
Priah appeared
in 2018's The Oath,

00:07:08.345 --> 00:07:10.180
a political comedy
about a family

00:07:10.264 --> 00:07:13.183
trying to survive a cursed
Thanksgiving weekend.

00:07:13.267 --> 00:07:15.352
Looking ahead,
Priah is set to star

00:07:15.435 --> 00:07:18.438
in Netflix's animated series
My Dad the Bounty Hunter

00:07:18.522 --> 00:07:21.316
and Marlon Wayans-produced
Halloween movie Boo.

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:23.277
Can I try
the peppermint stick?

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:25.529
Haven't you already tried
the peppermint stick?

00:07:25.612 --> 00:07:28.490
Yes, and I'd like
to try it again.

00:07:29.241 --> 00:07:30.659
So that's what
the increasingly

00:07:30.742 --> 00:07:32.536
inaccurately named
Stranger Things kids

00:07:32.619 --> 00:07:34.037
have been up to recently.

00:07:34.121 --> 00:07:36.790
Who are you most excited to
reconnect with in Season 4?

00:07:36.874 --> 00:07:38.208
Let us know in the comments,

00:07:38.292 --> 00:07:40.335
and remember to subscribe
to Still Watching Netflix

00:07:40.419 --> 00:07:43.255
for more videos about your
favourite shows and movies.

